{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-330332" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are both solutions of the homogeneous system\n${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t).$\nWhich of the following is **always** a solution of the same system?\n\n- $x(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)$\n- $x(t)=-4\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)$\n- $x(t)={e}^{2t}\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066703/state.json" "file_sha256" "7a8639649c43ccf473fc0212c91af3b4fdc66d39cbce10b1e9640246157aea6c"} {"question" "q-330332" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The *linearity principle* for systems of linear ordinary differential equations (ODEs) states that if ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are solutions to a homogeneous linear system, then for any constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2},$ the linear combination \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis also a solution of the system. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given expressions.\n\n- Option I might be *not* a solution to the system since it's not a scalar multiple of any of the solutions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$ Notice that the multiplier is not a constant.\n\n- Option II is a solution to the system. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n-4\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis a linear combination of the solutions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ with constant multiplies ${c}_{1}=0$ and ${c}_{2}=-4,$ respectively.\n\n- Option III might be *not* a solution to the system since it's not a scalar multiple of any of the solutions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066703/state.json" "file_sha256" "7a8639649c43ccf473fc0212c91af3b4fdc66d39cbce10b1e9640246157aea6c"} {"question" "q-330332" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066703/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "972875cb7ed570621eb3dc3196d9e76b3ef34c948aee263a74c9c045f4ab7dc3"} {"question" "q-330332" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066703/state.json" "file_sha256" "7a8639649c43ccf473fc0212c91af3b4fdc66d39cbce10b1e9640246157aea6c"} {"question" "q-330332" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"] ["text" "None"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066703/state.json" "file_sha256" "7a8639649c43ccf473fc0212c91af3b4fdc66d39cbce10b1e9640246157aea6c"} {"question" "q-330332" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066703/state.json" "file_sha256" "7a8639649c43ccf473fc0212c91af3b4fdc66d39cbce10b1e9640246157aea6c"} {"question" "q-330312" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are both solutions of the homogeneous system\n${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t).$\nWhich of the following is **always** a solution of the same system?\n\n- $x(t)={t}^{2}\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)$\n- $x(t)={x}_{1}(t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)$\n- $x(t)=-3\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+5\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066703/state.json" "file_sha256" "7a8639649c43ccf473fc0212c91af3b4fdc66d39cbce10b1e9640246157aea6c"} {"question" "q-330312" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The *linearity principle* for systems of linear ordinary differential equations (ODEs) states that if ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are solutions to a homogeneous linear system, then for any constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2},$ the linear combination \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis also a solution of the system. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given expressions.\n\n- Option I might be *not* a solution to the system since it's not a linear combination of the solutions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$ Notice that the multiplier is not a constant.\n\n- Option II might be *not* a solution to the system since it's not a linear combination of the solutions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$ Notice that the multiplier of the second term is not a constant.\n\n- Option III is a solution to the system. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n-3\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+5\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis a linear combination of the solutions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ with constant multiplies ${c}_{1}=-3$ and ${c}_{2}=5,$ respectively.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066703/state.json" "file_sha256" "7a8639649c43ccf473fc0212c91af3b4fdc66d39cbce10b1e9640246157aea6c"} {"question" "q-330312" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066703/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "972875cb7ed570621eb3dc3196d9e76b3ef34c948aee263a74c9c045f4ab7dc3"} {"question" "q-330312" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066703/state.json" "file_sha256" "7a8639649c43ccf473fc0212c91af3b4fdc66d39cbce10b1e9640246157aea6c"} {"question" "q-330312" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066703/state.json" "file_sha256" "7a8639649c43ccf473fc0212c91af3b4fdc66d39cbce10b1e9640246157aea6c"} {"question" "q-330312" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066703/state.json" "file_sha256" "7a8639649c43ccf473fc0212c91af3b4fdc66d39cbce10b1e9640246157aea6c"} {"question" "q-321646" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are both solutions of the homogeneous system\n${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t).$\nWhich of the following is **always** a solution of the same system?\n\n- $x(t)=2\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)$\n- $x(t)={x}_{1}(t)-t\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)$\n- $x(t)={x}_{1}(t)⊙{x}_{2}(t)$ (element-wise product)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066703/state.json" "file_sha256" "7a8639649c43ccf473fc0212c91af3b4fdc66d39cbce10b1e9640246157aea6c"} {"question" "q-321646" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The *linearity principle* for systems of linear ordinary differential equations (ODEs) states that if ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are solutions to a homogeneous linear system, then for any constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2},$ the linear combination \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis also a solution of the system. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given expressions.\n\n- Option I is a solution to the system. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n2\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+(-1)\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis a linear combination of the solutions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ with constant multiplies ${c}_{1}=2$ and ${c}_{2}=-1,$ respectively.\n\n- Option II might be *not* a solution to the system since it's not a linear combination of the solutions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$ Notice that the multiplier of the second term is not a constant.\n\n- Option III might be *not* a solution to the system since it's not a linear combination of the solutions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066703/state.json" "file_sha256" "7a8639649c43ccf473fc0212c91af3b4fdc66d39cbce10b1e9640246157aea6c"} {"question" "q-321646" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066703/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "972875cb7ed570621eb3dc3196d9e76b3ef34c948aee263a74c9c045f4ab7dc3"} {"question" "q-321646" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066703/state.json" "file_sha256" "7a8639649c43ccf473fc0212c91af3b4fdc66d39cbce10b1e9640246157aea6c"} {"question" "q-321646" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"] ["text" "None"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066703/state.json" "file_sha256" "7a8639649c43ccf